<!-- How Session Sandboxing Works Explainer Modal -->
<div id="sandbox-explainer-modal" class="modal-backdrop" hidden>
  <div class="modal-card" style="max-width: 680px;">
    <div class="modal-header">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem;">
        <span style="font-size: 1.3rem;">💡</span>
        <div>
          <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-primary);">How Session Sandboxing Works</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Stateful mock API testing without account registration or logins</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="modal-close-btn" id="close-explainer-modal-btn" title="Close Modal">&times;</button>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-body" style="padding: 1.5rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem;">

        <!-- Step 1 -->
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start;">
          <div style="background: var(--get-badge); color: #fff; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">
            1
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 style="margin: 0 0 0.35rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Automatic HMAC Identity Issuance</h4>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5;">
              On your very first request, the server generates a cryptographically signed <strong>HMAC-SHA256 identity token</strong> issued via an HTTP-only cookie (<code>pg_identity</code>) or <code>X-Playground-Identity</code> header. No sign-up or API key is required.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 2 -->
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start;">
          <div style="background: var(--post-badge); color: #fff; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">
            2
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 style="margin: 0 0 0.35rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Session Overlay Mutations</h4>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5;">
              When you issue <code>POST</code>, <code>PUT</code>, <code>PATCH</code>, or <code>DELETE</code> requests, your mutations are recorded into a private session sandbox (<code>overlay_records</code>). Shared global seed data remains untouched for all other developers.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 3 -->
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start;">
          <div style="background: #f59e0b; color: #fff; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">
            3
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 style="margin: 0 0 0.35rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Virtual Merging Engine</h4>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5;">
              Subsequent <code>GET</code> requests run through our Virtual Merging Engine. Your newly created records appear at the top, updates overlay in-place, and deleted items are filtered out specifically for your active session.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Features Summary Badge -->
      <div style="margin-top: 1.5rem; padding: 0.85rem 1rem; background: var(--bg-sidebar); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-muted); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <span>🛡️ Quota: 30 custom created records per resource</span>
        <span>⌛ Retention: 10-day inactivity cleanup</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-footer">
      <button type="button" id="dismiss-explainer-modal-btn" class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem;">
        Got it!
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
